title: materialize writes a config kanban-md refuses to load
updated: 2026-08-10T01:27:58Z
---

`karr materialize` is documented as the bridge to kanban-md. The config it
writes is rejected outright by the real binary:

    karr materialize && kanban list
      -> parsing config: yaml: unmarshal errors:
           line  6: cannot unmarshal !!int `1` into bool   (bypass_column_wip)
           line 27: cannot unmarshal !!int `1` into bool   (require_claim)
           line 29: cannot unmarshal !!int `1` into bool   (require_claim)
      # after hand-fixing the bools:
      -> invalid config: next_id must be >= 1              (key absent entirely)

Two independent blockers in `BoardStore.pm:232` (`DumpFile` of the merged config)
and `Config.pm:214-247`: Perl's `1`/`0` are dumped as YAML integers where
kanban-md expects `true`/`false`, and `next_id` is never materialized at all —
`serialize_from` even strips it (`BoardStore.pm:296`).

So the refs->files direction of the bridge does not work for its stated purpose.
Fix: emit real YAML booleans (JSON::PP::true / YAML::XS boolean handling) for the
boolean config keys, and write `next_id` into the materialized config.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
